    "field": "Coastal carbon cycle",
    "problem": "The diverse sources, sinks, and complex interactions of carbon in the coastal ocean remain poorly understood, making it challenging to accurately account for this dynamic and anthropogenically altered component within the global carbon budget.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a synthesis of observational data and biogeochemical models to re-evaluate the coastal carbon budget, concluding it has shifted from a carbon source to a sink due to increased physical uptake of atmospheric CO\u2082 and now represents an important zone of carbon transformation and sequestration.",
    "task": "The task is to synthesize current understanding of the sources, exchanges, and fates of carbon in the coastal ocean and how anthropogenic activities have altered its role in the global carbon budget.",
